    "https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26723": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor - German",
      "description": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal | Visiting Assistant Professor - German Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Visiting Assistant Professor - German Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates should apply for this position using this link https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26623 and submit the following materials: cover letter, vita, evidence of teaching excellence, transcript, two letters of recommendation, and writing sample. The committee will start reviewing applications on November 2, 2026. Materials or links that cannot be uploaded through the PeopleAdmin site may be e-mailed to mglee@unomaha.edu . For further information please contact Dr. Eugenio Di Stefano, Department of World Languages and Literature, University of Nebraska at Omaha, edistefano@unomaha.edu Posting Details Position Information Job Title Visiting Assistant Professor - German Department World Languages and Literature Essential Functions The University of Nebraska at Omaha seeks a full-time Visiting Assistant Professor ( VAP ) in German for an 18-month appointment to begin January 4, 2027. The successful candidate will teach four courses per semester (eight courses per academic year) at all levels of the German curriculum. The specialization is open; however, candidates should be a capable of teaching a wide variety of German language and culture courses. This position is not renewable. Significant experience and demonstrated excellence in teaching German at multiple levels, a focus on student retention, and expertise in the integration of technology in the classroom, especially in teaching both in-person and online modes, are essential. The successful candidate will be an enthusiastic and supportive participant in department activities, especially the German program’s weekly Stammtisch . The University of Nebraska Omaha is a Doctoral/Research institution with over 15,000 students. The German program, housed in the Department of World Languages and Literature offers an undergraduate BA. The University of Nebraska at Omaha is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to preventing and eliminating discrimination against employees and prospective employees based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. The University of Nebraska at Omaha does not condone or tolerate discrimination. In support of this policy, the University has implemented employment programs to recruit, employ, and promote qualified individuals based solely on their knowledge, skills, abilities and talents. These factors, along with our commitment to recruit, assess and select all candidates/employees using job-related criteria, ensure fairness, equal evaluation, and treatment in our selection decisions and processes. Work Schedule M-F; Occasionally the department hosts events on weekends, such as conferences and workshops. At times, classes are offered in the evening (after 4:30 pm) Additional Duties One department committee Required Qualifications Minimum qualifications: Native or near-native German language proficiency and a PhD or ABD status in German Studies, German literature, German linguistics, or related disciplines. ABD candidates should preferably have a defense date scheduled. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Regularly sits; may stand, walk. See, hear, speak and use of hands. Work Environment The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Regularly works indoors. Noise level is low to moderate. Salary Competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2026F-00152 Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates should apply for this position using this link https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26623 and submit the following materials: cover letter, vita, evidence of teaching excellence, transcript, two letters of recommendation, and writing sample. The committee will start reviewing applications on November 2, 2026. Materials or links that cannot be uploaded through the PeopleAdmin site may be e-mailed to mglee@unomaha.edu . For further information please contact Dr. Eugenio Di Stefano, Department of World Languages and Literature, University of Nebraska at Omaha, edistefano@unomaha.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Teaching Statement or Evidence Writing Sample Letter of Recommendation Optional Documents University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
