    "https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26700": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, DSW Director Appointment",
      "description": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal | Assistant/Associate Professor, DSW Director Appointment Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor, DSW Director Appointment Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your curriculum vitae applicants should provide a cover letter addressing professional experience relevant to the required and preferred qualifications as well as contact information for three references. Application review will begin on November 2, 2026 and continue until filled. For questions, please reach out to: Dr. Susan Reay, Director for the Grace Abbott School of Social Work, sreay@unomaha.edu or 402-554-2824 Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant/Associate Professor, DSW Director Appointment Department Grace Abbott School of Social Work Essential Functions This Assistant/Associate Professor faculty position serves as the Director of the Doctor of Social Work ( DSW ) program and plays a pivotal leadership role in the administration and advancement of the program. Key responsibilities include marketing the program and actively recruiting prospective students, overseeing the admissions process, and assigning incoming students to appropriate cohorts. The Director will teach three doctoral seminars/undergraduate courses and summer courses annually, evaluate comprehensive exams, and participate on all dissertation committees to ensure academic rigor and consistency. Additionally, the Director ensures timely completion of all requirements for students’ “Application for Admission to Candidacy,” manages student concerns and requests, and provides mentorship and support to faculty teaching within the DSW curriculum. This position requires a strategic and student-centered approach to program management, academic leadership, and faculty collaboration. Anticipated start date is August 16, 2027. About Us: The University of Nebraska at Omaha ( UNO ) is Nebraska’s only public metropolitan university, uniquely positioned at the heart of the state’s largest city. As a proud member of the University of Nebraska system, UNO offers a distinctive blend of academic excellence, impactful research, and meaningful community engagement, all within a student-centered environment that fosters opportunity, access, and achievement. With more than 15,000 students and a campus known for its variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences, UNO is committed to merit-based opportunity, inclusive excellence, and the transformative power of education. We emphasize experiential learning and innovation in all that we do, preparing our graduates to lead in a dynamic, global society. The University of Nebraska at Omaha is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to preventing and eliminating discrimination against employees and prospective employees based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. The University of Nebraska at Omaha does not condone or tolerate discrimination. In support of this policy, the University has implemented employment programs to recruit, employ, and promote qualified individuals based solely on their knowledge, skills, abilities and talents. These factors, along with our commitment to recruit, assess and select all candidates/employees using job-related criteria, ensure fairness, equal evaluation, and treatment in our selection decisions and processes. Work Schedule Additional Duties Required Qualifications Applicants must hold a PhD in Social Work or a Doctor of Social Work. Preferred Qualifications Doctor of Social Work preferred. A strong record of research and experience in education, including teaching using various modalities. A demonstrated record of significant community engagement is also preferred. Additionally, evidence of ability to build collegial working relationships with colleagues across multiple disciplines, campuses, and the community. Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Regularly sits; may stand, walk. See, hear, speak and use of hands. Work Environment The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Regularly works indoors. Noise level is low to moderate. Salary Commensurate with Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2026F-00134 Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants In addition to your curriculum vitae applicants should provide a cover letter addressing professional experience relevant to the required and preferred qualifications as well as contact information for three references. Application review will begin on November 2, 2026 and continue until filled. For questions, please reach out to: Dr. Susan Reay, Director for the Grace Abbott School of Social Work, sreay@unomaha.edu or 402-554-2824 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Teaching Statement or Evidence Research Statement University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26681": {
      "title": "Instructor - Social Work",
      "description": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal | Instructor - Social Work Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor - Social Work Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please submit the following: 1.) Cover letter 2.) CV 3.) Transcript (official or unofficial) from highest held degree. Review of applications will begin on October 19, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. For questions, please reach out to: Dr. Susan Reay, Director for the Grace Abbott School of Social Work, sreay@unomaha.edu or 402-554-2824. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Instructor - Social Work Department Grace Abbott School of Social Work Essential Functions The University of Nebraska at Omaha ( UNO ) invites applications for an instructor position in the Grace Abbott School of Social Work. This is a full-time, benefits-eligible, non-tenure position renewable on an academic year basis contingent upon satisfactory performance, availability of resources, and the enrollment needs of the university. Anticipated start date is January 4, 2027. This position is ideal for experienced social work practitioners and teaching-focused educators who are passionate about preparing the next generation of social workers through practice-informed instruction. The Instructor role emphasizes excellence in teaching, student mentorship, and integration of applied social work practice. Workload would be 12 credit hours fall and spring semesters with opportunities to serve on departmental committees. The University of Nebraska at Omaha is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to preventing and eliminating discrimination against employees and prospective employees based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. The University of Nebraska at Omaha does not condone or tolerate discrimination. In support of this policy, the University has implemented employment programs to recruit, employ, and promote qualified individuals based solely on their knowledge, skills, abilities and talents. These factors, along with our commitment to recruit, assess and select all candidates/employees using job-related criteria, ensure fairness, equal evaluation, and treatment in our selection decisions and processes. Work Schedule Additional Duties Required Qualifications Candidates must have an MSW plus a minimum of two years of practice experience. Preferred Qualifications Current social work licensure or license eligibility is preferred. Relevant social work practice experience or demonstrated expertise may include, but is not limited to: mental and behavioral health practice, crisis intervention, trauma-informed care, child welfare, work with immigrant and refugee populations, cross-cultural or community based social work. Experience teaching undergraduate and/or graduate social work courses is preferred, including in-person, hybrid, or distance education formats. Experience incorporating experiential learning, service learning, or community engagement, as well as commitment to working with under-served populations is preferred. Physical Demands Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Work Environment The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Regularly works indoors. Noise level is low to moderate. Salary Commensurate with Experience Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2026F-00111 Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please submit the following: 1.) Cover letter 2.) CV 3.) Transcript (official or unofficial) from highest held degree. Review of applications will begin on October 19, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. For questions, please reach out to: Dr. Susan Reay, Director for the Grace Abbott School of Social Work, sreay@unomaha.edu or 402-554-2824. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Resume University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
